1
00:00:27,361 --> 00:00:30,964
(Francesca Next Door)

2
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,635
(All names of people, places, events,
and other details are fictitious.)

3
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,969
(AI-based technology was used
in part of the production.)

4
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:39,907
(One day
before Pi Na Young's first day of school)

5
00:00:57,658 --> 00:00:58,659
This is...

6
00:01:02,629 --> 00:01:04,498
Where did you find that ax?

7
00:01:05,032 --> 00:01:06,300
- In the streets.
- Pardon?

8
00:01:11,638 --> 00:01:14,274
Oh, but why are you putting it here?

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:15,542
It's a decoration.

10
00:01:18,512 --> 00:01:19,980
I see your vision,

11
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,182
but you should put it back
to where you found it...

12
00:01:27,955 --> 00:01:29,122
Brilliant choice, miss.

13
00:01:34,795 --> 00:01:37,464
But are you really making me
live in a place like this?

14
00:01:38,432 --> 00:01:39,866
It's smaller than my bathroom!

15
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:43,103
I'm sorry, Ms. Francesca.
Please bear with it for now.

16
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:45,672
(Wi-Fi)

17
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,474
There's no Wi-Fi either.

18
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:50,844
I'll get your phone set up
as soon as I've earned some money.

19
00:01:50,911 --> 00:01:52,479
So please be patient.

20
00:01:52,546 --> 00:01:54,514
How do I live without the Internet?

21
00:01:54,815 --> 00:01:56,049
Why did it have to be this way?

22
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:57,551
That's because...

23
00:01:58,051 --> 00:02:00,554
your father invested
in the wrong cryptocurrency...

24
00:02:01,455 --> 00:02:03,190
What kind of currency is that expensive?

25
00:02:06,526 --> 00:02:08,161
Yeah, sorry about that.

26
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:15,369
The landlord agreed to lend you
this empty house for a bit,

27
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:17,704
so the water and power
are probably shut off.

28
00:02:18,605 --> 00:02:20,007
What about food?

29
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:26,880
You need to go to school.

30
00:02:27,214 --> 00:02:28,915
They have school lunches.

31
00:02:29,449 --> 00:02:31,551
It's free. You should be able to manage
one meal on your own.

32
00:02:32,119 --> 00:02:35,322
(Student ID
Pi Na Young, Dooil High School)

33
00:02:36,256 --> 00:02:37,257
Ms. Francesca.

34
00:02:38,091 --> 00:02:40,927
I'll come back for you
once we sort this out,

35
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:43,063
so please try to make do for now.

36
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:44,131
And lastly...

37
00:02:44,898 --> 00:02:46,867
Always keep this in mind.

38
00:02:47,534 --> 00:02:49,870
You should never let anyone know
that you're a vampire.

39
00:02:50,871 --> 00:02:52,005
The day anyone finds out...

40
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,176
What happens then?

41
00:03:22,703 --> 00:03:23,704
Call the emergency.

42
00:04:01,641 --> 00:04:02,642
I saw it right.

43
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:04,911
I definitely saw it.

44
00:04:05,979 --> 00:04:07,380
I'm not crazy.

45
00:04:08,115 --> 00:04:09,149
That was...

46
00:04:10,383 --> 00:04:11,451
What the heck?

47
00:04:12,552 --> 00:04:13,954
I was here first.

48
00:04:14,721 --> 00:04:15,722
Why did you run away?

49
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:18,425
You... What are you?

50
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:22,062
How did you just crack your neck back?

51
00:04:22,496 --> 00:04:24,164
Oh, that thing.

52
00:04:29,169 --> 00:04:32,472
I guess taking vitamins lately
helped me recover faster.

53
00:04:32,739 --> 00:04:35,375
You should also take them.
Vitamin C is good for skin renewal...

54
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:37,711
Stop with all that nonsense.

55
00:04:41,081 --> 00:04:43,183
Answer my question straight.

56
00:04:45,218 --> 00:04:46,219
What are you?

57
00:04:47,254 --> 00:04:48,255
An alien?

58
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:50,123
A ghost?

59
00:04:50,757 --> 00:04:51,825
Or is it...

60
00:04:54,561 --> 00:04:55,629
I'll make this clear.

61
00:04:56,463 --> 00:04:58,398
You didn't see anything today. Got it?

62
00:04:59,099 --> 00:05:01,835
If I hear you say one word
about me to anyone,

63
00:05:02,636 --> 00:05:03,637
you...

64
00:05:04,905 --> 00:05:05,906
will die.

65
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:07,741
All clear?

66
00:05:10,343 --> 00:05:11,344
Good.

67
00:05:11,411 --> 00:05:13,680
Then see you tomorrow, class president.

68
00:05:28,128 --> 00:05:29,129
Got it.

69
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:48,181
This crappy house doesn't even have Wi-Fi.

70
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:54,120
(September 1, Tuesday)

71
00:06:27,621 --> 00:06:29,856
(Where should we begin?)

72
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:33,326
(Can a person recover on their own
from a car accident injury?)

73
00:06:36,296 --> 00:06:38,031
(A human-like creature
with traits of another species)

74
00:06:38,098 --> 00:06:39,699
(Something entirely nonhuman)

75
00:06:48,375 --> 00:06:49,376
An alien?

76
00:06:50,543 --> 00:06:51,544
A ghost?

77
00:06:53,446 --> 00:06:55,382
Seriously, what is she?

78
00:07:00,487 --> 00:07:02,455
(Dalbit-ro)

79
00:07:14,067 --> 00:07:16,169
- What are you doing?
- Hey, class president.

80
00:07:17,938 --> 00:07:18,972
Did you follow me...

81
00:07:19,306 --> 00:07:20,540
to kill me?

82
00:07:20,907 --> 00:07:24,144
What are you talking about?
This spot has great Wi-Fi.

83
00:07:29,149 --> 00:07:30,150
Wi-Fi?

84
00:07:46,099 --> 00:07:47,567
Is it because of this?

85
00:08:05,785 --> 00:08:06,786
What?

86
00:08:09,222 --> 00:08:10,223
Class president!

87
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:12,826
Hey, open the door!

88
00:08:13,259 --> 00:08:15,328
- Did you set up a password? Unlock it!
- Just leave.

89
00:08:15,395 --> 00:08:17,397
Please get out of there.

90
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:20,500
Unlock it!

91
00:08:29,476 --> 00:08:30,477
Is she gone?

92
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,718
I'm so screwed.

93
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:43,456
(Dooil High School)

94
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:47,927
Hey, class president.

95
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:01,608
Despite his beloved's departure,

96
00:09:01,674 --> 00:09:03,743
the speaker hasn't accepted
the separation.

97
00:09:04,144 --> 00:09:07,247
Instead, he believes they'll meet again.

98
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:11,551
Toward the end of the verse,
his attitude changes...

99
00:09:12,419 --> 00:09:15,221
- Hey, class president. I'm...
- I should go to the restroom.

100
00:09:39,345 --> 00:09:40,480
- Are you avoiding me?
- Oh, jeez!

101
00:09:41,481 --> 00:09:42,515
Don't sneak up on me.

102
00:09:43,116 --> 00:09:44,250
Why are you avoiding me?

103
00:09:45,718 --> 00:09:46,786
I'm not.

104
00:09:47,153 --> 00:09:48,455
You have been all day.

105
00:09:48,922 --> 00:09:51,091
I told you not to spread the word,
not to hide from me!

106
00:09:53,793 --> 00:09:54,794
That's because...

107
00:10:04,471 --> 00:10:05,472
Password.

108
00:10:06,239 --> 00:10:08,007
- What?
- The Wi-Fi password.

109
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:10,844
You set it up, right? Unlock it.

110
00:10:11,911 --> 00:10:13,346
I don't know what you mean.

111
00:10:13,746 --> 00:10:14,848
Are you serious?

112
00:10:14,914 --> 00:10:18,651
Hey, I'm sorry, but I have to go.
I've got something to do.

113
00:10:28,995 --> 00:10:30,964
Why is it so hard to get
a little studying done?

114
00:10:36,569 --> 00:10:37,570
Hey, class president.

115
00:10:41,441 --> 00:10:43,610
She didn't look that dangerous.

116
00:10:45,411 --> 00:10:48,214
An alien or the Buddha,
it's none of my business.

117
00:10:49,115 --> 00:10:50,383
I shouldn't get involved.

118
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:52,652
I should just focus on the next mock exam.

119
00:10:53,052 --> 00:10:54,721
That's what I should be doing.

120
00:10:54,787 --> 00:10:56,022
- Class president.
- Yeah?

121
00:10:56,456 --> 00:10:57,490
Mr. Chung wants to see you.

122
00:10:59,058 --> 00:11:00,059
Excuse me?

123
00:11:00,126 --> 00:11:04,364
I noticed she actually listens
when you tell her something.

124
00:11:05,732 --> 00:11:07,834
But that's just not fair.

125
00:11:08,601 --> 00:11:10,770
Why should I tutor her?

126
00:11:11,571 --> 00:11:13,006
That's what you should do.

127
00:11:13,072 --> 00:11:15,542
I know it's my responsibility, but...

128
00:11:16,543 --> 00:11:20,547
I've had a lot on my plate
since becoming department head.

129
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:24,517
Trust me, I'm not asking you to do much.

130
00:11:24,884 --> 00:11:25,952
This coming mock exam,

131
00:11:26,419 --> 00:11:30,056
just help her get
an average score of at least 50.

132
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,125
You can do this.

133
00:11:33,092 --> 00:11:34,093
No, sir.

134
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,995
No matter how I look at it,
it doesn't seem right.

135
00:11:37,096 --> 00:11:38,097
I can't do it.

136
00:11:40,867 --> 00:11:41,868
U Ju...

137
00:11:43,269 --> 00:11:45,238
Aren't you running
for student council president next year?

138
00:11:46,139 --> 00:11:47,574
Hey, listen.

139
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,943
If you build some leadership skills,

140
00:11:50,009 --> 00:11:51,978
I can write you
a good recommendation letter...

141
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:53,813
for your student council
president election.

142
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:55,081
This would really help...

143
00:11:55,148 --> 00:11:58,017
with your college application
under the leadership category.

144
00:11:59,085 --> 00:12:00,486
Isn't med school your goal?

145
00:12:32,619 --> 00:12:34,721
Hey, Grass. Where's the class president?

146
00:12:35,722 --> 00:12:37,490
How would I know?

147
00:12:37,557 --> 00:12:38,591
I'm not even surprised.

148
00:12:39,626 --> 00:12:40,727
Where the heck is he?

149
00:12:41,094 --> 00:12:42,095
Are you looking for someone?

150
00:12:52,305 --> 00:12:53,373
What do you want?

151
00:12:53,573 --> 00:12:54,607
Me?

152
00:12:54,674 --> 00:12:56,276
I'm here to say hi to my friend.

153
00:12:56,743 --> 00:12:59,145
I thought both people had to agree
to be friends.

154
00:12:59,479 --> 00:13:00,813
I never agreed to this...

155
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:02,081
unless you plan on serving me.

156
00:13:02,415 --> 00:13:03,816
Let me give you some advice as a friend.

157
00:13:04,083 --> 00:13:05,084
Advice?

158
00:13:05,885 --> 00:13:07,854
Don't get too involved with the humans.

159
00:13:08,054 --> 00:13:09,689
I guess you're quite anti-social.

160
00:13:10,323 --> 00:13:11,324
Especially...

161
00:13:12,592 --> 00:13:13,593
him.

162
00:13:17,597 --> 00:13:18,598
Hey, class president.

163
00:13:18,731 --> 00:13:20,366
Come inside. I have something to tell you.

164
00:13:20,933 --> 00:13:21,934
Okay.

165
00:13:32,245 --> 00:13:33,413
(CSAT Workbooks)

166
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:34,881
What are these?

167
00:13:36,382 --> 00:13:38,351
These are the subjects
you should study from now on.

168
00:13:38,718 --> 00:13:39,719
Why should I?

169
00:13:40,687 --> 00:13:41,854
You'll kill me if I tell?

170
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:43,790
That means...

171
00:13:43,856 --> 00:13:45,658
you'd be in trouble
if your identity got out.

172
00:13:46,693 --> 00:13:47,827
I'll keep your secret,

173
00:13:48,361 --> 00:13:51,064
but only if you let me tutor you.

174
00:13:51,397 --> 00:13:54,334
I threatened you last night.
I didn't ask you for a favor.

175
00:13:56,469 --> 00:13:57,470
Do you really want to die?

176
00:14:03,109 --> 00:14:04,110
Go ahead.

177
00:14:04,310 --> 00:14:06,045
I'd rather die
than not get into med school.

178
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,680
Kill me, then.

179
00:14:08,414 --> 00:14:09,415
What?

180
00:14:09,716 --> 00:14:12,352
Whoever you are, I must make you study.

181
00:14:14,954 --> 00:14:16,055
I'm not asking for much.

182
00:14:17,590 --> 00:14:19,926
Try to get an average above 50.

183
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,061
It's easy.

184
00:14:22,595 --> 00:14:23,596
Just get half of them right.

185
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,975
Fine, but I have one condition.

186
00:14:36,609 --> 00:14:37,643
Which is?

187
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,545
You should be my butler.

188
00:14:39,612 --> 00:14:40,613
What?

189
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:42,281
Show me things, like you did yesterday,

190
00:14:42,348 --> 00:14:43,383
about the human world.

191
00:14:45,051 --> 00:14:47,120
Now you're openly admitting
you're not human.

192
00:14:47,186 --> 00:14:48,187
So?

193
00:14:48,454 --> 00:14:49,455
Are you in?

194
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,561
A guide.

195
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,097
I'll be your guide, not a butler.

196
00:14:59,098 --> 00:15:00,299
I have no intention of serving you.

197
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:03,269
Okay, fine.
Plus, give me the Wi-Fi password.

198
00:15:03,336 --> 00:15:05,071
What? That's a no.

199
00:15:05,138 --> 00:15:06,139
Then I won't cooperate.

200
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:11,744
How about this?

201
00:15:16,015 --> 00:15:17,483
(Connections)

202
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:19,285
(Mobile Hotspot and Tethering)

203
00:15:23,656 --> 00:15:25,258
(Wi-Fi
Universe's Galaxy)

204
00:15:26,559 --> 00:15:27,593
One hour a day.

205
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:30,163
I'll let you use it
if you study what I teach you.

206
00:15:32,665 --> 00:15:33,666
No more compromises.

207
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,301
If you don't like it,

208
00:15:35,902 --> 00:15:36,903
- do as you wish.
- Deal.

209
00:15:38,237 --> 00:15:39,238
Deal.

210
00:15:40,473 --> 00:15:43,209
We'll study at my place after school.

211
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:44,777
Until then,

212
00:15:45,711 --> 00:15:46,879
have a look at these.

213
00:15:48,581 --> 00:15:49,715
I don't think you will, but...

214
00:15:51,584 --> 00:15:54,086
Then until school ends,

215
00:15:55,388 --> 00:15:56,522
don't talk to me.

216
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:09,001
(Wi-Fi
Universe's Galaxy)

217
00:16:21,514 --> 00:16:22,515
Class president!

218
00:16:30,223 --> 00:16:32,325
Please. Do you have to be so loud?

219
00:16:32,792 --> 00:16:33,826
Why should I keep it quiet?

220
00:16:35,294 --> 00:16:36,963
Gosh, never mind.

221
00:16:37,029 --> 00:16:38,030
Come. Follow me.

222
00:16:47,273 --> 00:16:48,274
You might trip and fall.

223
00:16:48,875 --> 00:16:50,276
Shouldn't you tie your shoe?

224
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:51,377
I don't know how.

225
00:16:57,783 --> 00:16:58,784
Stop for a minute.

226
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:06,392
Didn't anyone teach you how to tie this?

227
00:17:07,059 --> 00:17:08,561
My butler does everything for me.

228
00:17:08,895 --> 00:17:09,896
I have nothing to do.

229
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:11,697
Your butler?

230
00:17:11,764 --> 00:17:12,798
So you have one at home?

231
00:17:13,199 --> 00:17:14,200
Not now.

232
00:17:14,267 --> 00:17:15,468
He's out for work.

233
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:17,036
My family went broke.

234
00:17:18,804 --> 00:17:19,805
What about your parents?

235
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:20,873
They're not here.

236
00:17:23,543 --> 00:17:24,844
- Do you live alone?
- Yes.

237
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:36,756
There.

238
00:17:39,325 --> 00:17:40,326
It's tied.

239
00:17:42,528 --> 00:17:45,264
I'll teach you
how to tie your shoes later...

240
00:17:45,331 --> 00:17:46,399
so you can do it yourself.

241
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:47,900
Okay.

242
00:17:55,041 --> 00:17:57,310
By the way, what's your real name?

243
00:17:57,977 --> 00:17:58,978
My real name?

244
00:17:59,512 --> 00:18:00,580
It should be Romanian, no?

245
00:18:01,347 --> 00:18:02,915
It can't be Pi Na Young.

246
00:18:03,449 --> 00:18:05,318
Oh, my real name is...

247
00:18:05,384 --> 00:18:08,287
Francesca Alexandra Cantemir Dumitrescu...

248
00:18:08,688 --> 00:18:11,257
Never mind. I'll just call you Na Young.

249
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:12,959
Okay.

250
00:18:21,167 --> 00:18:22,168
Come in.

251
00:18:35,014 --> 00:18:36,015
What are you doing?

252
00:18:37,917 --> 00:18:38,918
You have power.

253
00:18:46,158 --> 00:18:47,193
You have water!

254
00:18:49,762 --> 00:18:50,763
It's so cool.

255
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:55,201
It's better than my place.

256
00:18:55,935 --> 00:18:57,603
What kind of life are you living?

257
00:18:59,538 --> 00:19:02,041
Anyway, I'll bring the study materials.
Wait right here.

258
00:19:15,655 --> 00:19:17,456
Hey, I've been saving that!

259
00:19:18,891 --> 00:19:21,327
- Aren't you going to study?
- Why should I?

260
00:19:21,394 --> 00:19:23,362
I like it here. I'll just live here.

261
00:19:23,596 --> 00:19:25,431
The audacity to say that
in front of the host.

262
00:19:27,099 --> 00:19:28,401
Sit up. We have to study.

263
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:29,468
I don't want to.

264
00:19:34,573 --> 00:19:35,574
(Connections)

265
00:19:35,641 --> 00:19:37,009
(Mobile Hotspot and Tethering)

266
00:19:37,076 --> 00:19:38,511
(Off)

267
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:44,183
Hey!

268
00:19:44,984 --> 00:19:46,018
It's just an hour.

269
00:19:46,218 --> 00:19:47,586
Study hard for an hour,

270
00:19:47,653 --> 00:19:49,121
and I'll keep it on
for the rest of the day.

271
00:19:50,856 --> 00:19:53,025
So sit over there.

272
00:20:08,207 --> 00:20:09,842
Solve up to this question.

273
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:11,577
Ask me when you're stuck.

274
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:17,683
I have a question.

275
00:20:18,684 --> 00:20:19,685
What is it?

276
00:20:19,752 --> 00:20:22,822
Cheol Su gave 2 apples to Yeong Hui
when he had 5 at first.

277
00:20:23,723 --> 00:20:24,857
Why would he give them away?

278
00:20:27,426 --> 00:20:29,495
It's just a question.
You have to do the math.

279
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:31,731
Is that so?

280
00:20:38,871 --> 00:20:41,674
Cheol Su took 6 hours to finish a job
when Yeong Hui did it in 3 hours.

281
00:20:42,708 --> 00:20:43,976
Isn't he stupid?

282
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,412
I guess he's slow.

283
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:57,189
Cheol Su ran 3km to Yeong Hui's house,

284
00:20:57,957 --> 00:20:59,825
so how much does he love her?

285
00:21:04,296 --> 00:21:05,564
Are you doing this on purpose?

286
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:22,047
One hour is over. That's it for today.

287
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:26,051
Go home.

288
00:21:26,352 --> 00:21:27,720
No, I want to stay.

289
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:29,355
You'd better leave...

290
00:21:29,889 --> 00:21:31,624
if you want to get
even a single bar of signal.

291
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:51,043
Why is everyone in white except for you?

292
00:21:51,443 --> 00:21:52,444
They're all doctors.

293
00:21:54,647 --> 00:21:55,714
Doctors?

294
00:21:55,781 --> 00:21:56,949
You don't know what that is?

295
00:21:57,616 --> 00:21:58,617
I do.

296
00:21:58,684 --> 00:21:59,885
They help people heal.

297
00:22:00,352 --> 00:22:02,221
I never get hurt, so I've never met one.

298
00:22:03,355 --> 00:22:04,356
Right.

299
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:07,259
I have to go to med school
to become a doctor too,

300
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:09,662
and I have to tutor you
to get into med school.

301
00:22:11,697 --> 00:22:14,133
Why is tutoring me necessary
for you to get into med school?

302
00:22:16,468 --> 00:22:17,469
That's how it works.

303
00:22:18,604 --> 00:22:20,539
Sure, it's none of my business.

304
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:24,109
Anyway, I thought
doctors made a lot of money.

305
00:22:24,977 --> 00:22:27,046
Isn't this place a little shabby
for a family of doctors?

306
00:22:28,514 --> 00:22:29,582
Thanks for the compliment.

307
00:22:31,383 --> 00:22:32,685
It's our family tradition...

308
00:22:32,751 --> 00:22:35,387
to donate all our earnings
except for the living expenses.

309
00:22:35,988 --> 00:22:37,489
They have so much compassion for humanity.

310
00:22:39,859 --> 00:22:41,193
Now will you please go?

311
00:22:48,234 --> 00:22:49,702
Why do you want to be a doctor?

312
00:22:50,636 --> 00:22:52,137
Do you have someone you want to heal?

313
00:22:54,106 --> 00:22:55,107
No.

314
00:22:55,174 --> 00:22:56,542
Then why?

315
00:22:57,543 --> 00:22:58,544
That's because...

316
00:22:59,011 --> 00:23:01,580
my mom, dad, sister, and brother
are all doctors.

317
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:09,421
Does that mean you have to be one as well?

318
00:23:13,325 --> 00:23:14,326
That's not...

319
00:23:19,465 --> 00:23:20,833
Go home right now.

320
00:23:21,834 --> 00:23:23,102
But I don't want to.

321
00:23:23,168 --> 00:23:24,470
Please, I beg you.

322
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:31,243
See you, class president.

323
00:23:46,191 --> 00:23:48,193
(Dalbit-ro)

324
00:23:55,701 --> 00:23:57,670
(Butler Francisco)

325
00:23:59,071 --> 00:24:00,105
Ms. Francesca!

326
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,340
Oh, it's you.

327
00:24:01,674 --> 00:24:02,975
Why is it so hard to reach you?

328
00:24:03,042 --> 00:24:04,376
I was worried sick!

329
00:24:04,810 --> 00:24:06,245
I have no Wi-Fi.

330
00:24:06,312 --> 00:24:07,613
Get my phone activated already.

331
00:24:09,315 --> 00:24:10,516
Are you doing okay?

332
00:24:10,582 --> 00:24:11,617
How was school?

333
00:24:13,252 --> 00:24:14,820
Well, it's not bad.

334
00:24:14,887 --> 00:24:16,021
I have someone who looks after me.

335
00:24:16,221 --> 00:24:17,222
Looks after you?

336
00:24:18,724 --> 00:24:20,059
(Delivery order came in.)

337
00:24:20,125 --> 00:24:21,193
I got another one.

338
00:24:22,094 --> 00:24:24,463
Ms. Francesca, I have to get going.

339
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:25,731
Already?

340
00:24:29,168 --> 00:24:31,804
Ms. Francesca,
you have to keep a low profile...

341
00:24:32,171 --> 00:24:34,106
until I come back for you.

342
00:24:34,873 --> 00:24:37,676
Don't let anyone find out
that you're a vampire.

343
00:24:38,177 --> 00:24:39,178
Never.

344
00:24:39,912 --> 00:24:40,913
Oh, about that...

345
00:24:41,246 --> 00:24:42,247
(Call ended.)

346
00:25:01,433 --> 00:25:02,968
- Why are you so late?
- Oh, my gosh!

347
00:25:06,538 --> 00:25:07,539
What's going on?

348
00:25:07,806 --> 00:25:09,341
I can't charge my phone at home.

349
00:25:10,476 --> 00:25:11,543
What?

350
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:22,187
Oh, no.

351
00:25:24,523 --> 00:25:25,524
Why are you following me?

352
00:25:26,425 --> 00:25:28,060
The signal gets weak when you're too far.

353
00:25:28,460 --> 00:25:29,528
Don't move around so much.

354
00:25:31,130 --> 00:25:32,131
What are you saying?

355
00:25:37,169 --> 00:25:38,337
(Toilet
Man)

356
00:25:47,913 --> 00:25:48,914
What took you so long?

357
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:52,418
Hey, you...

358
00:26:06,732 --> 00:26:07,733
Don't move.

359
00:26:08,667 --> 00:26:09,668
Stay right there.

360
00:26:13,806 --> 00:26:14,807
I said, don't move.

361
00:26:20,379 --> 00:26:22,714
Keep this much space between us
outside of class.

362
00:26:25,117 --> 00:26:27,019
What's wrong with being close?
I didn't ask for anything.

363
00:26:27,453 --> 00:26:28,454
What I'm saying is...

364
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:32,858
It makes me really uncomfortable.
Stay away from me.

365
00:26:32,925 --> 00:26:33,926
Do you understand?

366
00:26:42,101 --> 00:26:43,769
Wait, that's not what I...

367
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:50,175
- A bug.
- What?

368
00:27:18,604 --> 00:27:19,905
Shouldn't you stay away from me?

369
00:27:25,911 --> 00:27:26,945
Hey...

370
00:27:27,012 --> 00:27:28,046
Anyway...

371
00:27:29,248 --> 00:27:30,315
Keep your distance.

372
00:27:30,382 --> 00:27:31,383
Okay?

373
00:27:56,241 --> 00:27:57,409
Aren't you eating that one?

374
00:28:13,158 --> 00:28:14,793
Don't go too far!

375
00:28:14,860 --> 00:28:16,695
It's hard to keep up with you!

376
00:28:41,019 --> 00:28:42,020
Is this thing...

377
00:28:43,689 --> 00:28:44,790
delicious?

378
00:28:45,691 --> 00:28:46,992
Give it to me if you don't like it.

379
00:28:48,660 --> 00:28:50,262
I know something
that tastes better than this.

380
00:28:52,264 --> 00:28:53,332
Don't you want to find out?

381
00:28:53,599 --> 00:28:54,800
You know something better?

382
00:28:57,603 --> 00:28:58,604
There's a ton.

383
00:29:00,839 --> 00:29:02,241
Something like human blood.

384
00:29:21,627 --> 00:29:22,761
Do I have something on my face?

385
00:29:23,729 --> 00:29:24,997
Why are you staring at me?

386
00:29:25,797 --> 00:29:28,066
You're the first of my kind I've met
besides my father.

387
00:29:29,668 --> 00:29:30,669
By the way,

388
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:33,438
do you really have some?

389
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:34,606
Have what?

390
00:29:37,743 --> 00:29:38,744
This?

391
00:29:40,045 --> 00:29:41,847
(Blood)

392
00:29:43,248 --> 00:29:44,349
So this is...

393
00:29:45,284 --> 00:29:46,285
What is it?

394
00:29:46,885 --> 00:29:47,986
Don't tell me.

395
00:29:48,687 --> 00:29:49,788
You've never had this?

396
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:54,793
My father said drinking human blood...

397
00:29:55,127 --> 00:29:56,295
was beneath us these days.

398
00:29:57,496 --> 00:29:58,497
"Beneath us?"

399
00:30:00,165 --> 00:30:01,166
Really?

400
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:07,639
I'll let you have it for free this time.

401
00:30:09,141 --> 00:30:10,242
Think of it as a friendship gift.

402
00:30:11,310 --> 00:30:14,546
Drink it or throw it away.
It's all up to you.

403
00:30:19,217 --> 00:30:20,218
Bye now.

404
00:30:37,202 --> 00:30:39,037
No, don't do it.

405
00:30:39,104 --> 00:30:41,273
It's uncivilized.

406
00:30:42,140 --> 00:30:43,275
It's disgraceful...

407
00:30:44,276 --> 00:30:46,211
as a vampire to...

408
00:31:13,672 --> 00:31:15,407
I've studied enough for today.

409
00:31:24,783 --> 00:31:25,784
But...

410
00:31:27,853 --> 00:31:30,155
she's probably somewhere around here.

411
00:31:34,393 --> 00:31:36,228
(Dooil High School)

412
00:31:36,294 --> 00:31:37,295
Pi Na Young?

413
00:31:45,036 --> 00:31:46,037
Where is she?

414
00:31:53,845 --> 00:31:54,846
You were here.

415
00:31:56,381 --> 00:31:57,482
Hey, let's go home.

416
00:32:06,191 --> 00:32:07,192
Did you hear me?

417
00:32:17,002 --> 00:32:18,003
Hey.

418
00:32:20,639 --> 00:32:21,640
I'm leaving.

419
00:32:28,346 --> 00:32:30,182
Gosh, my nose is bleeding.

420
00:32:30,715 --> 00:32:33,685
You're such a handful,
you're giving me a nosebleed.

421
00:32:34,519 --> 00:32:35,520
Do you have a tissue?

422
00:32:36,855 --> 00:32:38,056
Na Young?

423
00:32:38,490 --> 00:32:39,491
Oh, gosh.

424
00:32:41,359 --> 00:32:42,360
What's this now?

425
00:32:43,595 --> 00:32:44,596
What's wrong?

426
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:46,631
Are you okay?

427
00:32:47,599 --> 00:32:48,600
Just...

428
00:32:49,234 --> 00:32:50,235
Just one bite.

429
00:32:50,669 --> 00:32:51,670
What?

430
00:32:54,573 --> 00:32:56,208
Hey, snap out of it!

431
00:32:57,309 --> 00:32:59,244
Why are you...

432
00:32:59,744 --> 00:33:00,745
Na Young!

433
00:33:08,453 --> 00:33:09,454
Are you a vampire?

434
00:33:12,157 --> 00:33:13,158
What?

435
00:33:24,302 --> 00:33:25,303
You have...

436
00:33:26,071 --> 00:33:28,907
red eyes and sharp fangs.

437
00:33:30,308 --> 00:33:31,309
Hey...

438
00:33:32,477 --> 00:33:34,346
You're a vampire, right?

439
00:33:45,957 --> 00:33:48,260
(Francesca Next Door)

440
00:35:48,713 --> 00:35:50,715
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
